id: pm-vcs-b7cb
title: "Phase 6: scale"
description: "Scale and lifecycle for arbitrary files: stable file identities and PM attribution; fragment and pack storage; content-defined and fixed chunking; range reads; reachability; shallow and partial history; shared sparse instances; repository links and local layers; oplog-safe garbage collection; and typed obliteration as a separate authorized operation."
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:25.736Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T20:11:49.141Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: Stable FileIds survive moves and make PM-linked arbitrary files traceable across change IDs; Chunked binary content streams and range-reads without whole-file materialization and preserves content identity across compression; Sparse instances never silently omit merge conflicts or PM attribution and can share immutable storage safely; Links and layers preserve their committed-versus-local boundary; GC retains every ref/oplog-reachable object while authorized obliteration returns a typed state distinct from missing or corrupt content
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-tr2a,parent,"2026-07-31T06:28:27.963Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T23:36:00.202Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — stable file identities via content-addressed storage (engine/objects.ts); chunked binary content with content-defined and fixed chunking (engine/fragments.ts, test/fragments.test.ts, test/cdc-fragments.test.ts); range reads without whole-file materialization; sparse instances sharing immutable storage (engine/instances.ts); 784 tests pass with 100/100/100/100 coverage. REMAINS — manifest metadata is not bounded independently of totalLength (pm-vcs-8qyx still open: no multi-level manifest); local layers and typed obliteration are not implemented (pm-vcs-8xis still open); oplog-safe garbage collection is not visible in the engine. The epic has 3 open children (pm-vcs-8qyx, pm-vcs-8xis, and one other) that track these remaining pieces."
  "2026-10-14T20:01:16.138Z",codex-agent,"Phase 6 audit only; no Phase 6 implementation in this branch. Evidence is implementing code and real named tests; final full-suite gate will provide current execution receipts.\n| Criterion | Files | Test names | Assessment |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Stable FileIds survive moves and preserve PM/ChangeId attribution | engine/model.ts, engine/repo.ts, engine/attribution.ts | test/attribution.test.ts: stable file identities trace edits, moves, copies, deletion and PM associations; two branches retain distinct linked-file identities and PM associations through merge | Met in implementation and regression coverage |\n| Chunked binaries stream, range-read and retain content identity across compression | engine/fragments.ts, engine/manifest-pages.ts, engine/object-stream.ts, engine/objects.ts | test/fragments.test.ts: writing a file larger than any single buffer never holds more than a fragment in memory; a range read touches only the fragments overlapping the range; test/feature-edges.test.ts: real decompression verifies framing, payload length, type and hash and preserves filesystem errors; native restore coalesces small fragments, handles larger payloads and ranges avoid per-fragment buffer lists | Met in implementation and regression coverage |\n| Sparse instances do not silently omit conflicts or PM attribution; immutable sharing is safe | engine/instances.ts, engine/repo.ts, engine/attribution.ts | test/instances.test.ts: an out-of-view conflict fails visibly and leaves no state behind; committing a staged change outside the view is refused, never silently recorded; concurrent instances share objects but never overwrite each other's state; committing with an unresolvable PM item fails visibly and commits nothing | Met in implementation and regression coverage |\n| Links and layers preserve committed/local boundary | engine/composition.ts, engine/repo.ts | test/composition.test.ts: committed links retain exact identity and pin after branch movement, without copying payloads or credentials; private tracked and new overlays preserve edited bytes across checkout, never stage or change trees | Met in implementation and regression coverage |\n| GC retains ref/oplog roots; authorized obliteration is distinct from absent/corrupt | engine/gc.ts, engine/erasure.ts, engine/lifecycle.ts, engine/composition.ts | test/gc.test.ts: dry run and apply retain all ref namespaces, both oplog sides, staged content, series and fragment pages; oplog-only displaced history remains readable and undoable after collection; test/composition.test.ts: typed reads and verification distinguish missing and corrupt from obliterated content | Met in implementation and regression coverage |\nNo missing acceptance-criterion implementation found in this audit. Scale/lifecycle follow-ups already exist: pm-vcs-uploadretention for abandoned upload expiry and pm-vcs-d9m8 for self-host artifact growth. Reuse those items rather than creating duplicate work. These tests do not certify unmeasured production capacity."
  "2026-10-14T20:11:49.141Z",codex-agent,"Phase 6 lifecycle follow-up discovered while implementing forge history retention: pm-vcs-j7mz defines explicit authorized retirement of refs/forge-archive, review history and associated oplog transitions. Current preservation meets the GC reachability criterion, but bounded retained-history growth remains a separate operational gap. Existing pm-vcs-uploadretention covers abandoned uploads. Neither lifecycle policy is implemented in this Phase 5 branch."
body: ""
